<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Unofficial CF5 (DRG) example. NOT an official PhilHealth sample.
  Written for the PhilHealth PECWS 3.0 developer docs (see /reference/cf5-xml).

  Same claim as eclaims-minimal.xml:
  - pHospitalCode "123456" = eCLAIMS@pHospitalCode (DRG error code 509).
  - ClaimNumber "202609170001" = CLAIM@pClaimNumber (DRG error code 222).
    Using the hospital's own claim number is our recommendation, not a
    PhilHealth rule; the sources disagree (KI-45).
  - PrimaryCode "A90" (dengue fever) = the ICDCODE in the eClaims XML.
  - No secondary diagnosis and no procedure: a medical case whose eClaims XML
    has no RVS code. Both containers are still required, so they are sent empty.
  - NewBornAdmWeight is empty because the patient is an adult.
  - If you add a PROCEDURE, send Laterality="N" when no side of the body
    applies (Guide rev. 20250217, KI-05). Ext1/Ext2 take 1-9; whether blank
    values are accepted is not documented (KI-63).

  Valid against the standalone cf5/CF5.dtd (revision 20240604), checked with lxml.
  NOT valid against the "DRG E-Claims DTD" v1.3 printed in the Implementation
  Guide p. 17, which requires exactly one SECONDARYDIAG and at least one
  PROCEDURE (KI-06). This is the case KI-06 says to confirm, so send a file
  like this one to validateCF5 early.
-->
<CF5 pHospitalCode="123456">
  <DRGCLAIM ClaimNumber="202609170001" PrimaryCode="A90" NewBornAdmWeight="" Remarks="">
    <SECONDARYDIAGS/>
    <PROCEDURES/>
  </DRGCLAIM>
</CF5>
